  "findings": [
    "With loop closure enabled, RTAB-Map's position RMSE is 2.25x to 2.87x the custom stack's over the observed runs. The 2.88x reported from a single run each was at the optimistic end of that range.",
    "The custom stack's accuracy does not come from its loop closure. Disabling it leaves position RMSE unchanged at 0.0113 m; only yaw RMSE degrades, 0.0201 to 0.0285 deg. On this trajectory the ten committed constraints buy heading, not position.",
    "RTAB-Map's accuracy comes almost entirely from proximity detection. Without it its position RMSE is 0.1808 m, which is worse than the 0.1596 m odometry it consumes: its 1 Hz neighbour-link ICP does not improve on the EKF input on this data.",
    "Isolating the front ends therefore widens the gap rather than narrowing it: 13.42x to 17.47x with loop closure off, against 2.25x to 2.87x with it on.",
    "The custom stack is close to deterministic on fixed input: position RMSE 0.0113 m in all three runs and exactly 10 pose-graph commits each time."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Three runs per profile. The ranges are what three replays showed, not a confidence interval.",
    "One dataset and one trajectory. structured_loop_3d is a closed two-lap loop; a route without revisits would not exercise loop closure at all.",
    "RTAB-Map was not retuned beyond the detection-rate probe recorded in the superseded result; its front end may do better under a configuration not tried here.",
    "Turning proximity off removes RTAB-Map's only loop source but its neighbour-link refinement remains, so rtabmap_noloop is its front end as configured, not a bare scan matcher.",
    "The custom resource sampler covered scan_to_map_odometry_node only and omitted point_cloud_preprocessor_node. Custom CPU and RSS are historical lower bounds superseded by docs/results/2026-09-03-stack-resource-validation.json; the reported trajectory and loop distributions remain valid."
  ],
  "method": "Three replays per profile through map_projection_comparison.launch.py, all at the same revision. Every run consumes byte-identical sensor data and the same recorded odometry. Each trajectory is anchored to its own first sample and the estimate is read at the ground-truth stamp. The centre reported is the median with the observed range, because fixed input does not fix asynchronous loop verification and commit ordering.",
